 "summary": "The regular-expression dialect accepted by Google's RE2 library and its ports (Go's regexp, RE2/J): a Perl/PCRE-like syntax deliberately restricted to constructs matchable in linear time with automata (no backreferences or lookaround), with leftmost-first or POSIX leftmost-longest semantics.",
